WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.087
Hong Kong is a busy port city.

00:00:03.087 --> 00:00:05.974
For more than a hundred years, it was governed by Britain.

00:00:05.974 --> 00:00:10.256
Ferries came and went, shuttling across the harbor.

00:00:10.256 --> 00:00:14.895
In 1997, Hong Kong held a handover ceremony.

00:00:14.895 --> 00:00:19.049
Britain handed sovereignty over Hong Kong to the People's Republic of China.

00:00:19.049 --> 00:00:22.122
At the ceremony, representatives on both sides looked solemn.

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:25.585
At midnight, people gathered by the harbor.

00:00:25.585 --> 00:00:28.730
Fireworks lit up the night sky over Victoria Harbour.

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:33.683
Hong Kong became a Special Administrative Region, beginning a new phase.

00:00:33.683 --> 00:00:37.707
People's daily lives largely remained as before.

00:00:37.707 --> 00:00:41.696
Trams ran as usual, and cha chaan tengs stayed lively.

00:00:41.696 --> 00:00:44.743
'One country, two systems' was the core of the arrangement at the time.

00:00:44.743 --> 00:00:48.717
Hong Kong kept its own system and way of life.

00:00:48.717 --> 00:00:51.735
Many people cared about Hong Kong's future development.

00:00:51.735 --> 00:00:55.683
Hong Kong remained an important international city.

00:00:55.683 --> 00:00:59.504
This history influenced the direction of Hong Kong's future.
